  "match.rules.title": "How Equal stats works",
  "match.rules.1": "When it's on, the next unit you summon becomes the baseline, and its stats at spawn are recorded.",
  "match.rules.2": "Units summoned after it get the same max HP and Sha-Chi, attack, Sha-Chi damage and attack/defense multipliers, and enter with full HP and Sha-Chi.",
  "match.rules.3": "Moves, size, speed and AI don't change, so individual attacks can still deal different damage.",
  "match.rules.4": "If the baseline unit is hurt or dies, the baseline stays. After a full cleanup, the next unit you summon becomes the new baseline; a partial cleanup keeps it.",
  "match.rules.5": "Only units summoned afterwards by the app or its hotkeys are affected — not units already on the field, and not minions a boss calls in with its skills.",
  "match.rules.6": "Turning it off stops matching, and units on the field keep their current stats. Turning it back on picks a new baseline.",
  "match.rules.7": "If a unit can't be matched, it keeps its own stats and still fights. You'll see it under Activity.",
  "match.rules.8": "The game works out damage from level-1 base values, so those are matched to the baseline too; that is what makes units take and deal the same hits.",
